<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hook and Cod wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1350–1490</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hook and Cod wars were a series of factional conflicts in the County of Holland between about 1350 and 1490. They began in the succession dispute between Margaret of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> and her son William V, with the Hooks (Hoeken) backing Margaret and the Cods (Kabeljauwen) her son. The parties, drawn from nobles and towns, fought on through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacqueline-countess-of-hainaut">Jacqueline of Bavaria</a>'s struggle with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a> until the Burgundian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rulers subdued them.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hook-and-cod-wars.jpg" alt="Hook and Cod wars" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Rochussen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_Rochussen_-_Jacoba_van_Beieren,_het_veroverde_Gorcum_binnentrekkende,_ontmoet_het_lijk_van_Willem_van_Arkel_-_DM-878-205_-_Dordrechts_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
